 Schedule Risk Analysis
 Model Activity/Task Durations as Uncertain Quantities that have Probability Distributions
 Combine Activity/Task Durations Statistically (Monte Carlo simulations) to Generate
Cumulative Distributions of Project Total Duration
 Obtain confidence level dates to determine additional amount of time to complete project
 Identify best and deterministic date and probability of project completion date.
 *Stephen A. Book. “Schedule Risk Analysis: Why It is Important and How to Do It. March
2002.
 Discrete schedule risk mapping.
 Schedule risk factor mapping.
